---
// The player tier's CSS: the TIER block, the top-of-sheet line and the CAREER
// line on the sheet (PlayerSheet.astro), and the squad row's mark and its key
// (the team page). The rules are the design's (player-tiers design/mock),
// tokens only: no new colour, size or font.
//
// Inline, and rendered by the team page only when the tiers are, for one
// reason: with the publication gate closed the built site must be the site as
// it was before tiers existed (tiers.config.ts). A scoped <style> in the sheet
// or the team page is bundled whether or not anything uses it, which changes
// the stylesheet every page links to; this block exists in the output only on
// a page that draws a tier. Its class names are the tier's own, so being
// unscoped reaches nothing else.
---

<style is:inline>
  .tier-status { margin: 0; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); }
  .tier-meaning { margin: 0; font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--secondary); }
  .tier-basis { margin: 0; font-size: 12px; color: var(--secondary); }
  /* The team figures, in the CAREER grid's type: 12px/600 figures under a
     10px/0.1em head. A real table, so a screen reader moves by cell. */
  .tier-team { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 4px; font-size: 12px; }
  .tier-team caption {
    text-align: left; caption-side: top; padding: 0 0 4px;
    font-size: 10px; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--quiet);
  }
  .tier-team th, .tier-team td { padding: 3px 0; font-weight: 600; text-align: right; }
  .tier-team thead th { font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--quiet); font-weight: 400; }
  .tier-team tbody th { text-align: left; font-weight: 400; color: var(--secondary); }
  .tier-team td { width: 76px; }
  .tier-team td.tier-div { color: var(--secondary); font-weight: 400; }
  /* Goals given up against what the opponents usually score: one sentence
     under the table, in its row heads' register (Decision 2). */
  .tier-goals { margin: 0; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--secondary); }
  .tier-note { margin: 0; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--quiet); }
  /* The source line is the house's provenance sentence; the link in it wears
     PersonLink's hairline in the surrounding ink and takes the accent only on
     hover. Purple at rest would mean Touchline, and this is a footnote. */
  .tier-source { margin: 0; font-size: 12.5px; }
  .tier-link {
    color: inherit; text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--outline-quiet);
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px; text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .tier-link:hover { color: var(--accent); text-decoration-color: currentColor; }
  .tier-link:focus-visible { outline: 1px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
  /* Under a finger the padding takes the hit area and the equal negative
     margin gives the line back, as the header's views do. */
  @media (pointer: coarse) {
    .tier-link { display: inline-block; padding: 15px 0; margin: -15px 0; }
  }
  /* A holder's tier at the top of the sheet: its own line under the chip and
     the programme, so a wrap can never open a line on a separator; the size
     and grey of .sheet-where beside it. Plain text, not a link: a link into
     the sheet would change the hash, and the sheet opens on :target. */
  .sheet-tier { flex-basis: 100%; font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--secondary); }
  /* Earlier seasons' tiers, under the career note, in words. */
  .career-tiers { font-size: 12px; color: var(--quiet); }
  /* The squad mark: a 5px square turned 45°, drawn and never type, the same
     for every tier and both kinds. Not a dot (a hometown abroad), not hollow
     (a class year never printed). The words are in a .vh span beside it. */
  .squad-tier {
    flex: none; width: 5px; height: 5px; align-self: center;
    background: var(--quiet); transform: rotate(45deg); margin: 0 1px;
  }
</style>
